                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='8'>Source: </run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='8'>Data compiled from LABLAC (CEDLAS and the World Bank). </run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                        <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='8'>Note:</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='8'> Breaks in the series represent survey methodological changes. Productive definition of informality refers to the proportion of workers in small firms, non-professional self-employed workers, and zero-income workers. Social protection definition of informality refers to the proportion of salaried workers without pension benefits for all countries except Mexico and Peru, where it represents workers without health benefits. Wage employment is defined as the percentage of workers who are salaried.</run>
                        <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                        <run fontcolor='#555555' fontname='Tableau Light' fontsize='8' italic='true'>*Argentina only has urban coverage. Updated June 2025.</run>
